WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.506 --> 00:00:06.506
Orcas.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.776
Often known as killer whales.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:13.880
They stalk the oceans of the world,
living up to their infamous name.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.851
They hunt in groups
and use language to communicate.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.121
With their high intelligence,

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.723
they leave a trail
of terror in their wake.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:28.228
Now, it's they and not their prey
who are threatened.

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:33.033
Wildlife cameraman, David Reichert,
is determined to get intimately close

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.736
to this mighty predator
in its natural environment

00:00:36.303 --> 00:00:40.640
to understand firsthand the relationship
between the orca and its prey.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.202
In the southern Indian Ocean

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:14.007
midway between the coast of South Africa
and the Antarctic, lie the Crozet Islands.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.814
This French archipelago sits smack
in the middle of the Roaring Forties.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.449
Westerly winds that pack a real punch.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.353
Here it rains 310 days a year.

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:32.092
Winds in excess of 60 miles an hour
for much of the year

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.893
make human life unbearable.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.998
The wind brings rain, snow, and hail.

00:01:39.066 --> 00:01:42.803
On the Crozet Islands, you can experience
all four seasons in less than a day.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.807
September marks the beginning
of spring in the Southern Hemisphere,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:51.210
but there's never a good time
to venture into this region.

00:01:52.513 --> 00:01:53.580
Some people do.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.682
This longline fishing boat
is after a catch

00:01:56.884 --> 00:01:58.652
that can only be found in these waters.

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.454
Patagonian toothfish.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:04.024
They were only discovered
at the turn of the last century.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:08.261
Today, they fetch high prices
on dinner tables in Asia and America,

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:11.397
where they're more commonly known
as Chilean sea bass.

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.169
Other hunters prize the toothfish,

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:19.205
like the giant
of the dolphin family, the orca.

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:26.546
David Reichert is passionate about orcas
and intrigued by their behavior.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.251
Like all the fish around here,

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.087
the toothfish fish
swim too deep for whales and dolphins.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.490
But the amazing thing
is the orcas are such opportunists

00:02:37.658 --> 00:02:40.826
that they've adapted to the presence
of longline boats in the area.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:42.895
They've discovered an easy way to feed.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.632
They only have to wait
for the lines to be pulled up.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:03:00.613
Unfortunately,
a lot of pirate longliners are out there.

00:03:01.315 --> 00:03:04.518
They're illegal and try to force
the orcas to keep their distance

00:03:04.585 --> 00:03:06.352
by throwing dynamite at them.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:10.824
So the orcas have become
rather cautious towards human beings,

00:03:11.158 --> 00:03:13.593
even though they haven't given up
on the easy pickings.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.996
Scientists have produced alarming figures.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:21.434
Fifty percent of the orcas in the region
have disappeared in the last decade.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.404
It's a wanton and secret slaughter
by men without scruples.

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:33.613
David boarded one of the few
legal longliners to get to the islands

00:03:33.914 --> 00:03:36.283
and study the behavior
of this threatened mammal

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.684
in its natural environment.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:44.490
As a specialist in filming marine mammals,

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.061
David stops at nothing
to get close to his subjects.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.968
But what he's about to do
has never been attempted before.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:59.873
Filming underwater close to boats
that present a threat to the orcas.

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:02.708
How nervous will they be of his presence

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.078
if private fishermen
have struck in the past?

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:24.531
A young female approaches,
naturally inquisitive.

00:04:30.704 --> 00:04:32.673
Her mother instantly recalls her.

00:04:33.207 --> 00:04:36.476
In orca society,
the young don't need to be told twice.

00:04:48.989 --> 00:04:51.123
The orcas are certainly avoiding David.

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:55.494
He'll have to wait
until he gets to the Crozet Islands

00:04:55.562 --> 00:04:56.730
for another encounter.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.032
That's where the orcas are heading

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:03.903
because their traditional prey in the area
are not toothfish, but elephant seals.

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:19.286
Every spring,
elephant seals must return to dry land

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:22.455
to mate and give birth
after hunting at sea in the Antarctic.

00:05:24.191 --> 00:05:25.592
Over thousands of years,

00:05:26.026 --> 00:05:29.263
orcas have perfected
peculiar techniques to catch seals.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:38.171
I wonder how far
the presence of the longline boats

00:05:38.238 --> 00:05:41.507
has altered the orcas' culture
from generation to generation?

00:05:42.242 --> 00:05:44.110
Has it changed their feeding habits?

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:47.114
What impact has the slaughter really had?

00:05:48.315 --> 00:05:52.052
Has the elephant seal population
grown as the number of orcas declined?

00:05:56.156 --> 00:05:57.157
To find out,

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.561
David will spend four hard months
alongside these animals

00:06:00.627 --> 00:06:03.730
in conditions where life
is a daily struggle for survival.

00:06:14.441 --> 00:06:16.276
Here animals are safe from man.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:18.545
They shouldn't be afraid of people.

00:06:19.513 --> 00:06:21.714
It's the perfect place
to study their world

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:25.484
and understand the close links
that unite predator and prey.

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:31.257
I've arrived just in time.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.260
The elephant seals have begun to return.

00:06:38.966 --> 00:06:42.402
This 15 foot male seal
has spent 10 months at sea,

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:44.971
gorging on fish
and squid in the Antarctic.

00:06:46.006 --> 00:06:47.975
He's swum thousands of miles to get here.

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:51.878
Now, hauling four tons of blubber
onto dry land,

00:06:52.446 --> 00:06:54.247
only one thing is on his mind.

00:06:54.648 --> 00:06:55.648
Sex.

00:06:57.251 --> 00:06:58.252
Enter a female.

00:06:58.819 --> 00:07:00.087
But she's not here to mate.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.091
Rather, to give birth to a pup
she conceived on the island last year.

00:07:05.492 --> 00:07:08.729
For the male,
she's an irresistible image of Aphrodite.

00:07:10.664 --> 00:07:15.269
To reproduce, males must establish
a harem and become the dominant male.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.104
The only way to do that.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:20.841
Throw your weight around
and impose yourself on other males.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:25.846
The male is six or seven times
heavier than the female,

00:07:26.113 --> 00:07:28.881
and to show he means business,
he bites her viciously.

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:30.516
How affectionate.

00:07:37.424 --> 00:07:41.227
The dominant male must keep
his trophies away from prying rivals.

00:07:44.264 --> 00:07:47.501
This potential rival
is already calculating the odds.

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:55.242
The role of dominant male
is highly coveted,

00:07:55.509 --> 00:07:58.144
and on this beach,
there's only room for one.

00:07:58.812 --> 00:08:00.414
Conflict is inevitable.

00:08:10.424 --> 00:08:11.825
Another female arrives.

00:08:12.726 --> 00:08:17.664
Distracted by the advances of two males,
she doesn't see the danger until too late.

00:08:25.506 --> 00:08:27.207
Her long journey is over.

00:08:27.875 --> 00:08:29.842
She'll never give birth to her pup.

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:36.984
Hunting this way shows how the orcas
have adapted to life around these islands.

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:41.655
Fish are rare and inaccessible,
so they must hunt marine mammals.

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:50.429
The rest of the family
has been alerted to the catch.

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:58.572
Allowing the others to join
the kill is a form of initiation,

00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:00.007
especially for the young.

00:09:00.507 --> 00:09:02.208
To survive, you must learn,

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:06.046
and the transmission of knowledge
is an essential part of orca culture.

00:09:14.955 --> 00:09:16.455
This might seem cruel,

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:20.093
but it shows the extent
to which orcas are social animals

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:22.562
and how far they go to protect each other.

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:34.174
The fatal blow
is delivered by a young female.

00:09:48.789 --> 00:09:53.192
Skuas and other scavenging birds
pluck raw protein straight from the sea.

00:09:58.465 --> 00:09:59.666
Home away from home.

00:10:00.734 --> 00:10:04.203
The wooden crate contains everything
David needs for his own survival

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:07.007
until the longline returns in four months.

00:10:13.614 --> 00:10:15.716
Skuas confirm David's suspicions.

00:10:19.119 --> 00:10:22.689
Animals on the Crozet Islands
have never been threatened by man.

00:10:23.924 --> 00:10:27.494
They've no reason to be aggressive,
but every reason to be curious.

00:10:33.533 --> 00:10:36.703
This is the price David
must pay to secure a front row seat

00:10:36.836 --> 00:10:39.306
to study how orcas
and their prey interact.

00:10:54.955 --> 00:10:57.991
Within a few days,
the dominant male elephant seal

00:10:58.057 --> 00:11:01.695
succeeds in pressing
large numbers of female into his harem.

00:11:02.729 --> 00:11:05.031
The problem now is to keep the peace.

00:11:21.914 --> 00:11:23.317
It's time for a nap.

00:11:30.924 --> 00:11:32.758
Others never seem to rest.

00:11:35.094 --> 00:11:38.465
There's always a chance of a fat seal
may be napping close to the edge.

00:11:45.304 --> 00:11:49.242
A large male orca with its typical
six-foot triangular dorsal fin

00:11:49.442 --> 00:11:53.013
is followed by two females
with their smaller, curved fins.

00:12:02.856 --> 00:12:04.958
Orcas live in a matriarchal society.

00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:09.362
The dominant female leads the group,
comprised from her sisters,

00:12:09.596 --> 00:12:12.466
daughters and other youngsters,
but never couples.

00:12:13.599 --> 00:12:16.203
Reproduction only takes place
between separate groups.

00:12:29.216 --> 00:12:31.151
The matriarch is very imposing.

00:12:31.552 --> 00:12:32.953
Over 20 feet long.

00:12:33.719 --> 00:12:36.656
I know orcas
have never been known to attack humans.

00:12:37.291 --> 00:12:41.127
But what if she really is eyeing me
for her next meal?

00:12:47.166 --> 00:12:50.103
The group moves off peacefully
to the south of the island.

00:12:56.809 --> 00:12:59.213
David's close encounter
with the orca on land

00:12:59.679 --> 00:13:03.116
reminds him of something
that happened on this beach in 1988.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:07.054
Amateur footage of the drama,
seen around the world,

00:13:07.588 --> 00:13:11.190
showed an inexperienced orca
becoming beached while hunting.

00:13:13.159 --> 00:13:16.296
But scientists were on hand
to help it back into the water.

00:13:19.666 --> 00:13:23.804
The female's release was a joy to behold
for both the scientists and the orcas.

00:13:24.104 --> 00:13:25.705
A very lucky escape.

00:13:37.317 --> 00:13:40.387
I wonder if the female
I encountered along the shore,

00:13:40.921 --> 00:13:43.090
could be the same one
the scientists saved.

00:13:43.924 --> 00:13:47.693
I felt threatened, but she may
only have wanted to make contact.

00:13:49.395 --> 00:13:51.864
What do I really represent
to these super predators?

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.601
It's a question that dogs me.

00:14:01.375 --> 00:14:05.078
This male seal knows only too well
what he represents for the orcas.

00:14:05.812 --> 00:14:08.247
He recently barely escaped
becoming a meal.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.854
Ironically, seals are more vulnerable
on land than they are at sea.

00:14:15.388 --> 00:14:19.793
They dive to depths of over 4,000 feet,
far deeper than any orca.

00:14:28.367 --> 00:14:31.038
In the shallows,
their thick layer of blubber

00:14:31.104 --> 00:14:33.005
offer a tempting feast of protein.

00:14:33.573 --> 00:14:36.409
No wonder orcas risk beaching
and hunting this way.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:41.481
But even close to shore,
the elephant seal is no pushover.

00:14:48.288 --> 00:14:49.922
A young orca strays from the group,

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:53.125
and finds itself face to face
with a powerful opponent.

00:14:56.429 --> 00:14:58.432
The orca hazards a closer inspection.

00:15:00.132 --> 00:15:01.567
The seal holds its ground.

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:11.143
No point in being too brave.

00:15:14.414 --> 00:15:16.283
It was a good lesson for the youngster.

00:15:16.783 --> 00:15:20.453
Next time, it'll stay with the group
where there's strength in numbers.

00:15:34.367 --> 00:15:39.505
This male is staking out his territory
even though it hasn't found a single mate.

00:15:54.721 --> 00:15:56.289
Hey, watch it.

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:58.424
Whoa, okay, calm down.

00:16:01.528 --> 00:16:03.330
Loneliness is obviously getting to him.

00:16:10.604 --> 00:16:12.539
It's time for me to explore the island.

00:16:13.273 --> 00:16:16.309
I've decided to cross
the little volcano to the other side,

00:16:16.643 --> 00:16:19.679
where I've noticed the orcas
disappear to a number of times.

00:16:43.637 --> 00:16:45.471
What is it that attracts them down there?

00:16:49.208 --> 00:16:50.943
This is the perfect spot for me.

00:16:53.346 --> 00:16:57.351
The rocky bottom leaves the water clear,
and for once, the sea is calm.

00:16:58.151 --> 00:17:00.052
What a treat
in this turbulent part of the world.

00:17:12.666 --> 00:17:15.334
It's now obvious to David
what the orcas are after

00:17:15.435 --> 00:17:16.603
on this side of the island.

00:17:18.604 --> 00:17:21.807
A sloping beach shelters
a colony of king penguins

00:17:21.875 --> 00:17:23.243
in their tens of thousands.

00:17:24.244 --> 00:17:28.814
For the orcas, the beach represents
a well-stocked larder all year round.

00:17:37.691 --> 00:17:40.427
Adult penguins
surround chicks born last year.

00:17:49.269 --> 00:17:52.005
They'll keep their warm,
woolly coats for about nine months.

00:17:59.011 --> 00:18:01.248
When they grow real feathers
and strong muscles,

00:18:01.714 --> 00:18:03.717
they'll take to the sea
to feed themselves.

00:18:14.193 --> 00:18:17.264
They wait patiently
for their parents to return with food.

00:18:28.208 --> 00:18:30.677
There are plenty
of distractions to kill time.

00:18:48.328 --> 00:18:49.796
They seem to have adopted me.

00:18:50.563 --> 00:18:51.932
Probably because they're hungry.

00:19:02.576 --> 00:19:04.610
Raising the young takes almost a year,

00:19:04.811 --> 00:19:07.114
and requires
great devotion from the parents.

00:19:08.548 --> 00:19:11.051
Mothers and fathers are away for ten days.

00:19:11.685 --> 00:19:13.921
They swim hundreds of miles
to their hunting grounds

00:19:14.154 --> 00:19:17.291
and dive 1,500 feet
to find fish and shellfish.

00:19:18.525 --> 00:19:21.128
Once they filled their crop,
they return to their young,

00:19:21.594 --> 00:19:24.765
picking them out from the crowd
by listening for their call.

00:19:38.411 --> 00:19:41.647
King penguins
take to the sea together for protection.

00:19:50.357 --> 00:19:55.027
This is an opportunity for orcas to refine
their coordinated hunting techniques.

00:20:07.173 --> 00:20:09.510
First, they observe complete silence.

00:20:10.811 --> 00:20:13.680
The hunters don't want
to sow panic among the penguins.

00:20:15.749 --> 00:20:17.683
Then, moments before the attack,

00:20:18.118 --> 00:20:21.454
they emit discrete clicks
to signal their position to each other.

00:20:25.491 --> 00:20:28.629
When the trap is set,
the matriarch sounds the signal.

00:21:00.494 --> 00:21:04.063
Catching a penguin demands
a lot of energy for little in return.

00:21:04.797 --> 00:21:07.600
But they haven't much choice
if there's nothing else to hunt.

00:21:12.505 --> 00:21:14.374
In summer, when the seals are abundant,

00:21:14.708 --> 00:21:17.744
hunting penguins is good practice
for the leaner winter months.

00:21:44.604 --> 00:21:47.274
For the penguins who managed
to break through enemy lines

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:48.509
to fish for their chicks,

00:21:49.109 --> 00:21:51.444
the return journey
proves equally perilous.

00:22:20.006 --> 00:22:23.677
Finally, starving chicks
are rewarded for their patience.

00:22:46.833 --> 00:22:48.836
September draws to a close.

00:22:49.635 --> 00:22:53.373
The dominant male now has
more than 100 females in his harem.

00:22:54.374 --> 00:22:57.311
This record number probably
has something to do with the fact

00:22:57.411 --> 00:22:59.046
that there are fewer orcas around.

00:22:59.613 --> 00:23:02.015
But orcas keep piling on the pressure,

00:23:02.548 --> 00:23:03.683
and for good reason.

00:23:04.183 --> 00:23:07.354
Female seals are about
to give birth to tender pups.

00:23:20.433 --> 00:23:23.870
Skuas and giant petrels
feast on the placenta.

00:23:29.343 --> 00:23:33.280
And anxious mothers
make sure the placenta is all they get.

00:23:36.483 --> 00:23:40.286
The first exchange of cries
between mother and baby are vital.

00:23:40.587 --> 00:23:44.423
Along with their odor, this allows them
to identify each other in the colony.

00:23:47.693 --> 00:23:49.062
With its eyes barely open,

00:23:49.896 --> 00:23:53.567
baby seals feed off the richest milk
of any mammal in the world.

00:23:54.868 --> 00:23:58.271
It contains ten times
more fat and calories than cow's milk.

00:23:59.706 --> 00:24:02.708
Pups put on four times their weight
in only three weeks.

00:24:03.142 --> 00:24:05.312
After that, mother's job is done.

00:24:08.614 --> 00:24:12.318
The dominant male tires of herding
ever more females into his harem.

00:24:13.487 --> 00:24:17.357
Not only must he watch over them,
but he must fertilize them too.

00:24:22.029 --> 00:24:25.232
This earthly paradise
comes with a price, starvation.

00:24:26.265 --> 00:24:29.603
The dominant male stops eating
for the entire reproductive season.

00:24:30.571 --> 00:24:33.573
He sheds 30 pounds every day
for two and a half months,

00:24:34.274 --> 00:24:35.776
surviving on his winter reserves.

00:24:36.510 --> 00:24:38.879
The ten months
spent feeding in Antarctica.

00:24:42.114 --> 00:24:44.750
Single males lie in wait
for the slightest opportunity.

00:24:45.953 --> 00:24:47.386
The presence of so many females

00:24:47.787 --> 00:24:50.390
stimulates their own desire
to perpetuate their genes.

00:24:53.693 --> 00:24:55.328
The dominant male cries foul.

00:24:55.928 --> 00:24:58.332
His bulbous nose amplifies the protest.

00:24:58.865 --> 00:25:01.767
The larger the nose,
the greater the show of virility.

00:25:03.069 --> 00:25:06.406
It's a rude instrument of dissuasion
for the legions of young pretenders.

00:25:11.043 --> 00:25:14.515
Seeing one intruder off
only lets another into the harem.

00:25:16.015 --> 00:25:18.484
What a never ending battle to stay on top.

00:25:20.052 --> 00:25:22.522
DNA studies show the dominant male

00:25:22.588 --> 00:25:24.891
is far from being the father
of all the pups.

00:25:41.275 --> 00:25:44.510
The hormonal urge
to mate leads to outright war.

00:26:58.985 --> 00:27:01.755
Winner takes all
in a clash between titans.

00:27:13.534 --> 00:27:15.536
When you get this close to these giants,

00:27:15.836 --> 00:27:17.537
you can feel how much energy

00:27:17.604 --> 00:27:20.239
goes into their drive
to pass on their genes.

00:27:21.240 --> 00:27:24.311
It's a symbol of resistance
to the extreme conditions of the place.

00:27:25.244 --> 00:27:26.646
A real fight for life.

00:27:27.947 --> 00:27:32.452
I'm determined to experience the same kind
of intense contact with the orcas.

00:27:33.654 --> 00:27:35.956
I'm going back
to the clear waters on the other side.

00:28:07.553 --> 00:28:10.723
I recognize the matriarch
by her imposing size.

00:28:11.224 --> 00:28:14.360
I see in the fullness
of her attention towards me

00:28:14.628 --> 00:28:17.797
great experience
and certainly a knowledge of man.

00:28:19.967 --> 00:28:22.235
Is she again the one
who was saved by the scientists?

00:28:23.203 --> 00:28:24.770
I like to imagine she is.

00:28:25.472 --> 00:28:27.473
I wish this moment would last forever.

00:28:28.407 --> 00:28:31.712
I must find out more about her
and her pod.

00:28:39.552 --> 00:28:42.522
Once again,
the orcas treat David with caution.

00:28:52.232 --> 00:28:55.769
The orcas developed a complex culture
because they live so long.

00:28:56.203 --> 00:28:58.204
Males live for about 50 years.

00:28:58.604 --> 00:29:00.707
Females can survive into their 80s,

00:29:01.041 --> 00:29:03.709
which explains
why their society is matriarchal.

00:29:04.244 --> 00:29:06.245
Females have more experience.

00:29:13.453 --> 00:29:15.588
These mammals are such efficient killers.

00:29:16.123 --> 00:29:19.092
They only need to spend
10% of their time hunting.

00:29:20.394 --> 00:29:23.563
Otherwise they rest,
play, and educate the young.

00:29:24.063 --> 00:29:26.432
A process that can last 20 years.

00:29:28.234 --> 00:29:31.104
Touching, caressing,
and talking maintains harmony.

00:29:33.072 --> 00:29:35.776
Scientists now know
that orcas from the same region

00:29:36.076 --> 00:29:37.510
share a common language,

00:29:38.045 --> 00:29:42.416
and even more amazing,
every individual clan has its own dialect.

00:30:06.707 --> 00:30:10.644
Frustrated on land,
David decides it's time for a dip.

00:30:20.487 --> 00:30:23.524
He hopes to meet orcas
in their own territory

00:30:23.589 --> 00:30:25.625
behind this bed of giant kelp.

00:30:52.318 --> 00:30:55.255
Orcas never venture
into these underwater forests.

00:30:56.322 --> 00:30:59.526
Solid stalks rise
120 feet from the bottom,

00:30:59.927 --> 00:31:02.462
and could become
a lethal trap for the orcas.

00:31:25.853 --> 00:31:29.355
Beyond the forest,
the matriarch sneaks up on David.

00:31:42.836 --> 00:31:46.607
Her clicks signal her position
to the others waiting in the shadows.

00:31:50.109 --> 00:31:52.880
The matriarch
is simply checking the visitor out.

00:31:57.250 --> 00:31:59.586
Once again, the encounter is fleeting.

00:32:00.286 --> 00:32:03.123
Caution and mistrust
seem to reign in the orcas.

00:32:07.895 --> 00:32:11.999
The appearance of penguins means the orcas
must have retreated to a safe distance.

00:32:20.941 --> 00:32:25.011
For David, their grace and agility
are well worth staying underwater

00:32:25.078 --> 00:32:26.145
for a little longer.

00:33:13.760 --> 00:33:16.796
Well, well, looks like I've got a visitor.

00:33:22.369 --> 00:33:26.206
The single male has been well
and truly defeated by the dominant male.

00:33:27.406 --> 00:33:29.208
Perhaps, next year he'll have more luck.

00:33:30.543 --> 00:33:32.845
Even the strongest seals
don't become dominant

00:33:32.946 --> 00:33:34.748
until they're at least eight years old.

00:33:35.082 --> 00:33:37.384
Even then,
for no more than two years running.

00:33:38.151 --> 00:33:40.720
The battle to dominate
exhausts them too much.

00:33:42.755 --> 00:33:46.359
He may not look aggressive,
but he's still potentially dangerous.

00:33:47.293 --> 00:33:49.363
There's no way
I can get into my tent tonight.

00:34:13.520 --> 00:34:15.455
What a beautiful day for a change.

00:34:16.123 --> 00:34:17.591
It does wonders for my mood.

00:34:26.666 --> 00:34:29.269
Baby elephant seals pass their first days

00:34:29.535 --> 00:34:31.637
close to the warm bellies
of their mothers.

00:34:32.471 --> 00:34:33.906
What momentary bliss?

00:34:34.842 --> 00:34:37.477
The atmosphere
on the beach is positively festive.

00:34:51.490 --> 00:34:54.961
Orcas also take advantage
of the peace and quiet to sleep.

00:34:55.662 --> 00:34:57.998
But the way they sleep is most unusual.

00:34:58.799 --> 00:34:59.833
So they don't drown,

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.769
evolution has blessed them
with an extraordinary trait.

00:35:03.370 --> 00:35:05.771
Only half their brain sleeps at one time.

00:35:06.606 --> 00:35:09.242
They literally nap with one eye open.

00:35:18.318 --> 00:35:22.289
No sooner has the sun come out,
than spring is on the back burner again.

00:35:31.264 --> 00:35:33.566
The Roaring Forties
return with a vengeance.

00:35:46.479 --> 00:35:49.315
Wisely, the orcas move away from shore.

00:36:32.525 --> 00:36:36.095
I wonder how the newborn elephant seals
are coping with the weather.

00:36:42.436 --> 00:36:45.438
The pups keep on suckling
as though nothing was wrong.

00:37:00.520 --> 00:37:02.089
It is really picking up.

00:37:03.189 --> 00:37:04.591
I'd better seek some shelter.

00:37:18.971 --> 00:37:21.774
Filming in these conditions
leaves me paralyzed with cold.

00:37:23.677 --> 00:37:25.211
Without the tent, I'd be finished.

00:37:26.145 --> 00:37:28.147
Suddenly, I feel very alone.

00:37:28.916 --> 00:37:30.917
Very different from the animals.

00:37:31.685 --> 00:37:33.520
I'm fragile and vulnerable.

00:37:36.123 --> 00:37:38.392
The storm turns
the beach into another world,

00:37:38.892 --> 00:37:40.093
or the end of the world.

00:37:40.760 --> 00:37:44.230
There seems no limit to the power
of the elements on the Crozet Islands.

00:38:21.667 --> 00:38:25.539
I've spent the night terrified
by the thought my tent would blow away.

00:38:29.476 --> 00:38:30.611
By mid-October,

00:38:31.410 --> 00:38:34.614
the first female elephant seals
to have arrived from the Antarctic

00:38:34.680 --> 00:38:35.815
are now ready to return.

00:38:37.885 --> 00:38:39.987
After nursing their pups for three weeks,

00:38:40.287 --> 00:38:43.724
they're pregnant again
and will give birth here in a year's time.

00:38:45.992 --> 00:38:49.530
This one is ready to leave,
but her pup isn't.

00:38:59.873 --> 00:39:02.608
Abandonment before weaning seems cruel.

00:39:03.343 --> 00:39:04.677
But there's a good reason.

00:39:05.412 --> 00:39:08.549
Mother no longer has the reserves
to continue producing milk,

00:39:09.016 --> 00:39:11.150
though she might return
after putting on weight.

00:39:13.553 --> 00:39:15.289
But time is not on her side.

00:39:16.689 --> 00:39:18.258
She's exhausted and vulnerable.

00:40:05.771 --> 00:40:07.773
Orcas share the spoils of hunting.

00:40:08.509 --> 00:40:11.210
Solidarity within the group
is a cardinal virtue.

00:40:25.525 --> 00:40:27.293
The pup too is a victim.

00:40:27.895 --> 00:40:30.129
How will it survive without its mother?

00:40:36.537 --> 00:40:39.873
Unlike penguin chicks
that can count on both parents for food,

00:40:40.573 --> 00:40:43.209
baby seals depend solely on their mothers.

00:40:57.690 --> 00:40:58.725
Weak and skinny,

00:40:59.193 --> 00:41:01.195
the orphan barely has a chance,

00:41:01.460 --> 00:41:02.762
even against a bird.

00:41:06.767 --> 00:41:08.435
It must find another mother.

00:41:14.675 --> 00:41:15.809
The door is closed.

00:41:16.443 --> 00:41:19.812
Female seals cannot afford
to feed two pups at once,

00:41:21.814 --> 00:41:25.352
and other pups also insist
on exclusive rights to their mothers.

00:41:43.803 --> 00:41:47.841
I'm heartbroken to see firsthand
the tragedy of this pup's life.

00:41:49.041 --> 00:41:50.677
But there's nothing I can do to help.

00:41:55.215 --> 00:41:58.318
It's been attacked
and rejected by its own species.

00:41:59.252 --> 00:42:01.955
A victim of the cruel laws
of natural selection.

00:42:03.189 --> 00:42:05.024
It will never know the taste of fish.

00:42:05.658 --> 00:42:07.326
Will never become a dominant male

00:42:07.561 --> 00:42:10.998
to father offspring
on this island at the end of the world.

00:42:29.383 --> 00:42:32.785
Mid-November and the harem
dissolves like snow in the sun.

00:42:35.289 --> 00:42:39.125
The dominant male rouses himself
one last time to perform his duty.

00:42:52.539 --> 00:42:54.842
Babies are now
fully weaned and independent.

00:42:56.275 --> 00:42:59.413
The young stick together
and discover the joys of infancy.

00:43:05.652 --> 00:43:06.919
They've begun to molt.

00:43:08.354 --> 00:43:11.524
Black at birth,
their fur has turned light gray,

00:43:13.025 --> 00:43:15.028
but the new coats itch terribly.

00:43:22.468 --> 00:43:24.670
David can't resist lending a hand.

00:43:25.205 --> 00:43:28.441
After all, they've been neighbors
for nearly four months.

00:43:36.049 --> 00:43:38.519
I know, it's not very scientific of me,

00:43:38.885 --> 00:43:41.922
but I just can't resist
these furry, little bodies.

00:43:46.626 --> 00:43:51.031
My excuse is that they, and not I,
made the first move into my camp.

00:43:51.931 --> 00:43:54.935
I'm really excited by their willingness
to let me into their lives.

00:44:24.397 --> 00:44:26.466
The seals really have accepted me.

00:44:26.934 --> 00:44:27.935
What an honor.

00:44:28.468 --> 00:44:31.170
The confidence they show
in me and the games they share

00:44:31.504 --> 00:44:34.675
are the simplest and most important
forms of communication.

00:44:35.843 --> 00:44:38.878
Moments like this
take me back to my own childhood.

00:45:07.273 --> 00:45:11.410
By December, hunger forces
the young seals into troubled waters.

00:45:12.712 --> 00:45:15.249
Their first tentative steps
are harmless enough.

00:45:15.716 --> 00:45:17.116
But unlike young orcas,

00:45:17.483 --> 00:45:21.121
they can't rely on adult protection
and education to survive.

00:45:27.427 --> 00:45:30.396
For some,
the baptism will be ruthlessly short.

00:45:39.706 --> 00:45:41.808
Orcas must fatten up for the winter ahead

00:45:41.875 --> 00:45:45.044
when measly penguins
will be all that's left on the menu,

00:45:45.645 --> 00:45:49.349
unless they brave the dynamite
to steal toothfish from the longliners.

00:45:51.584 --> 00:45:54.854
David must catch the young seals
in the water for the first time

00:45:54.955 --> 00:45:57.291
before they too migrate to the Antarctic.

00:46:21.314 --> 00:46:24.518
I was looking for him,
but in the end, he found me.

00:47:12.365 --> 00:47:14.935
Is he admiring me or mocking me

00:47:15.034 --> 00:47:17.803
for needing this ridiculous suit
to enter his world?

00:47:19.239 --> 00:47:20.806
But who's to say we can't be friends?

00:47:24.243 --> 00:47:25.511
If only he would stay.

00:47:28.549 --> 00:47:30.083
Why is he leaving?

00:47:31.518 --> 00:47:33.052
Will he be back?

00:47:36.757 --> 00:47:39.158
The answer is in black and white.

00:47:44.498 --> 00:47:46.767
Is she hoping to catch my seal friend?

00:47:54.106 --> 00:47:56.510
A male approaches me for the first time.

00:47:56.944 --> 00:48:00.479
He's nearly 30 feet long
and weighs more than eight tons.

00:48:00.914 --> 00:48:02.315
A living juggernaut.

00:48:05.284 --> 00:48:06.719
Then the matriarch returns.

00:48:07.287 --> 00:48:09.423
This time I'm sure
it's to make real contact.

00:48:35.681 --> 00:48:38.251
I feel naked and completely defenseless.

00:48:38.852 --> 00:48:42.789
The orcas know it too,
and I'm counting on their wisdom now.

00:48:43.156 --> 00:48:44.458
We are communicating.

00:48:44.925 --> 00:48:48.028
I don't know how exactly,
but it's pretty intense.

00:48:59.639 --> 00:49:06.012
In this open, smiling face, I realize
we have both exorcized our mutual fears.

00:49:22.428 --> 00:49:23.629
Call it intuition,

00:49:23.964 --> 00:49:28.602
but I'm now positive this female
is the one saved from the beach long ago.

00:49:29.468 --> 00:49:32.572
She's become head of the clan
and wants to know more about me

00:49:32.638 --> 00:49:35.541
before exposing
the others to potential danger.

00:49:36.409 --> 00:49:38.612
Today, she knows I come in peace.

00:49:52.625 --> 00:49:58.197
No words can express the emotion I feel
in such a sublime moment of contact.

00:50:12.545 --> 00:50:15.147
The orcas we sometimes call killer whales,

00:50:15.749 --> 00:50:17.316
may be in their own way,

00:50:17.583 --> 00:50:20.287
trying to thank us
for saving one of their own.

00:50:34.268 --> 00:50:37.637
I'm reassured to see
how the orcas of the Crozet Islands

00:50:37.905 --> 00:50:39.706
are preserving their ancient ways.

00:50:40.207 --> 00:50:43.110
For now, at least,
in spite of the longliners.

00:50:50.250 --> 00:50:52.752
Given their experience
at the hands of the pirates,

00:50:53.153 --> 00:50:55.789
their initial reaction
to me was to be cautious.

00:50:56.590 --> 00:50:57.591
How can you blame them

00:50:57.657 --> 00:51:01.228
when faced with such a destructive species
as humankind?

00:51:03.596 --> 00:51:05.531
Even when
their future is threatened by us,

00:51:06.032 --> 00:51:08.334
they show
just how discriminating they are.

00:51:08.602 --> 00:51:11.071
They opened the door
of their kingdom to me.

00:51:13.639 --> 00:51:17.076
On an island, where life hangs
in the balance every moment,

00:51:17.277 --> 00:51:19.879
wild animals accept my presence.

00:51:20.847 --> 00:51:24.784
They give up some of their secrets,
and embrace me with full confidence.

00:51:25.853 --> 00:51:29.423
This extraordinary encounter
has changed me.

00:51:30.323 --> 00:51:31.324
Forever.

